WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.310
Usually, Lev Ponomaryov spends his days in
the office fighting for human rights.

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:08.580
He helps those who've been unjustly imprisoned
get released.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.070
But today his desk is empty.

00:00:11.070 --> 00:00:16.039
Ponomaryov himself has been taken into custody
and faces 25 days in prison.

00:00:16.039 --> 00:00:21.570
The government accused him of using facebook
to incite protests supporting imprisoned activists.

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:26.650
In this publication, Ponomaryov supports parents
who are organising a demonstration for the

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:33.100
rights of their daughter who has been accused
of extremist activities against the state.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:37.410
This accusation was formulated with the help
of the Russian secret service.

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:40.829
At least that's what Oleg Elanchik and his
colleagues think.

00:00:40.829 --> 00:00:42.960
That's why they're here today.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:47.670
The 28-year-old would have never thought,
that he'd have to help his boss get out of

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:48.719
prison.

00:00:48.719 --> 00:00:53.460
Elanchik sets out to where Lev Ponomaryov
is being held.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:56.379
Here he meets up with Ponomayov's lawyer.

00:00:56.379 --> 00:00:59.399
We will file complaints.

00:00:59.399 --> 00:01:04.120
We hope that the court will correct their
mistakes in the second appeal.

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:10.350
Representatives of human rights organisations
have come to the prison in a show of solidarity.

00:01:10.350 --> 00:01:14.520
The government wants to scare activists and
all those who go to events where people fight

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:15.759
for human rights.

00:01:15.759 --> 00:01:19.159
For them, the process is politically motivated.

00:01:19.159 --> 00:01:24.250
That is why they are fighting it with political
as well as legal methods.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:27.510
Many people are visiting him and bringing
him things that he needs in prison.

00:01:27.510 --> 00:01:32.860
We are also going to the European Court to
protest his imprisonment.

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:37.990
They plan on doing everything they can to
help Lev Ponomarjov be freed.

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:41.320
One of the first reactions came from Mikhail
Fedotov.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:44.390
He is the head of President Putins human rights
council.

00:01:44.390 --> 00:01:49.170
Fedotov criticized the verdict, which he called
'inexplicable'.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:53.469
Amnesty international and other human rights
organizations condemned the imprisonment of

00:01:53.469 --> 00:01:54.810
Ponomarev as well.

